WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.179 --> 00:00:06.120
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for my bonus video I wanted to try and describe

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:16.650
each of The Doctor’s 13 Faces in the simplest
terms possible starting with William Hartnell.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.109
1 - The Wizard

00:00:18.109 --> 00:00:22.280
William Hartnell described his Doctor was
something of a cross between The Wizard of

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.920
Oz and Father Christmas.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.250
I guess you could make a joke about Smoke
and Mirrors leading to unexpected gifts.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.730
Paul McGann, the 8th Doctor described him
as having a very Victorian demeanor.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.690
But I prefer thinking of him as a Wizard.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.660
One of his most notable catchphrases was Come
Along My Dear.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.840
His closest personal connection was to his
granddaughter Susan Foreman, but he had all

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.210
the idiosyncrasies associated with an old
man.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:52.030
He had something of a mean streak in him and
was deeply mistrustful of outsiders.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.129
Just like the Wizard of Oz, he eventually
softened and began to enjoy spending time

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:00.410
with his companions and did not want to go
when it was time to regenerate.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.079
2 - The Clown

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:05.890
If the first Doctor had a much more victorian
personality, the second doctor swung to the

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.450
other end of the spectrum.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.890
His catchphrase was “When I say Run, Run!”

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.590
He was still every bit as clever and manipulative
but he would often play the fool to defeat

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:18.090
enemies or just be plain funny.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.840
He also panicked a lot despite being quite
heroic at all times.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.650
I like to think of it as a precursor to “The
Doctor Lies”.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.680
The Second Doctor was also really notable
for playing the recorder and his love affair

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.010
with hats.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.190
Something Matt Smith’s Doctor took from
quite a bit.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.670
3 - The Scientist

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:42.100
The Third Doctor was actually hired by Unit
as their Science Advisor.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.480
So he was very literally a scientist.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.560
During Jon Pertwee’s run, they constructed
a science lab standing set.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.950
The Doctor had been exiled by the time lords
and had to look for a place on earth to haunt.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:00.600
The First Doctor described him as a Dandy
because of his extravagant costume, but the

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.970
Third Doctor was far more physically active
than both of his previous selves.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:06.979
Like he became the karate master.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:12.349
During his run, he also became a master diplomat,
mediating disputes for the time lords.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:15.530
One of his more notable catch phrases was
“Now Listen to me!”

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.680
He’s also one of the few Doctor’s to drive
a car.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.469
4 - The Bohemian (Have a Jelly Baby?)

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:24.769
He was a genuinely warm and funny Doctor if
not just a little bit Manic.

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:28.969
I wouldn’t say manic depressive, but he
did have a much more cruel attitude towards

00:02:28.969 --> 00:02:32.799
the Time Lords.

00:02:32.799 --> 00:02:36.160
As the term implies, his costume and habits
were very adventuresome.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.590
He wandered around more than any other Doctor.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.849
Which technically isn’t fair, because he
got more episodes than any of the other Doctors.

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:46.779
His biggest catch phrase was “Have a Jelly
Baby?”

00:02:46.779 --> 00:02:49.909
He was a lot more aloof than the previous
doctor’s, and given to brooding.

00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:55.019
But I feel like he delivered some of the best
monologues in classic who.

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:59.040
He still retained a lot of the physicality
of the third doctor and even engaged in some

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.459
expert swordplay.

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:05.730
5 - The Pacifist

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:10.560
The fifth doctor was so against violence that
it eventually got him killed.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.450
He was probably one of the most sensitive
incarnations and dropped a lot of the eccentric

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.870
behaviors of the fourth Doctor.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:21.780
His biggest catch phrase was Sorry Must Dash,
but catch phrases in general weren’t as

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.200
prominent during his run.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.319
Like I said, dropping a lot of the eccentricities.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:30.120
Steven Moffat himself explained the Fifth
Doctor as being one of the most tortured,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.610
maybe not as much as the 9th Doctor, but Peter
Davison conveyed a lot of the emotional problems

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.999
of the Doctor in his performance.

00:03:37.999 --> 00:03:44.849
He was also one of the first boyish appearing
doctors, anachronistic to his extreme old

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:47.239
age.

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:50.510
6 - The Egoist

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.529
It may have been a result of his troubled
regeneration, but the Sixth Doctor had the

00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:57.260
worst mood swings of any of the other doctors.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:01.419
He was wildly egotistic and at the same time
compassionate.

00:04:01.419 --> 00:04:06.930
His most notable catch phrase was “I Wonder,
Ah Ha!”

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:13.089
His costume of wild colors is a good indicator
for the changes in his moods.

00:04:13.089 --> 00:04:16.639
Of all the Doctor’s costumes I feel like
his was one of the most polarizing.

00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:21.489
Some feel like it was disastrous and some
totally love it.

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:23.840
7 - The Chessmaster (Not This Time…)

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.229
The seventh doctor brought back a lot of the
silly behaviors of the second doctor as a

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:30.979
way to misdirect people from his true intentions.

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:34.530
He was generally one of the more curious,
inquisitive and charming doctors.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.970
And a consummate showman.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:36.990
Something which I think Capaldi is also trying
to bring back.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:40.539
One of his more notable catch phrases was
“Not This Time…”

00:04:40.539 --> 00:04:44.090
He was a noted chessmaster, actually playing
chess.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:48.639
But his adventures became an allegory for
a giant chess match against evil.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:51.789
The actually had a giant chessboard in this
week’s episode.

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:53.849
8 - The Romantic (Who Am I?)

00:04:53.849 --> 00:04:56.699
The Eighth Doctor was one of the most passionate.

00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:59.650
And one of the first to actually kiss his
companion.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:03.990
He suffered something of an identity crisis
post-regeneration and his most notable catch

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.629
phrase became “Who Am I?”

00:05:07.629 --> 00:05:10.909
Because of his very short run on television,
he didn’t really get much of a chance to

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:12.210
develop as a character.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:16.030
But the expanded material including the novels
and the audio dramas totally picked up the

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.030
slack.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:21.060
Which is why everyone crapped their pants
when he showed up in the Night of The Doctor.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.190
9 - The Warrior (No More…)

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:27.490
This was the dark doctor, we only saw him
at the very end of the time war, so most of

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:35.150
the supposed atrocities he committed in the
name of the Time Lords are left to speculation.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:42.900
But they’re bad enough that all the newer
Doctor’s refused to mention his name.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:47.879
His most notable catch phrase was “No More”

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:53.440
Steven Moffat said that he wrote John Hurt’s
Doctor thinking that the world was robbed

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:59.599
of a large period in the 90s when the show
was off the air.

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:03.440
During the story planning it’s said that
Moffat didn’t feel like the 8th Doctor would

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.969
have been the one to end the time war, it
just wasn’t in that character’s nature.

00:06:06.969 --> 00:06:12.539
And he was pretty certain Christopher Eccleston
would decline any invitation to come back.

00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:17.599
Thus John Hurt’s War Doctor was created.

00:06:17.599 --> 00:06:21.990
It’s crazy to think that had Christopher
Eccleston come back, he would have gotten

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.750
the John Hurt storyline in the 50th Anniversary.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.960
They would have had McGann regenerate into
Eccleston, then have eccleston detonate the

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.520
moment and escape in the TARDIS.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.759
10 - The Survivor

00:06:34.759 --> 00:06:39.190
The 9th Doctor was until recently, the last
survivor of the Time War, although Russell

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.729
Davies retconned that story so that the Master
and the Time Lords could come back.

00:06:42.729 --> 00:06:45.430
Then the 50th also changed all of it again.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:50.460
He was the PTSD doctor, given to violent outbursts
of joy and anger.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.949
His most notable catch phrase was “Fantastic!”

00:06:51.949 --> 00:07:01.810
Fans are still hoping that someday eccleston
will relent and come back for a future anniversary

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.810
special.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.449
11 - The Human

00:07:05.449 --> 00:07:13.430
The 10th Doctor was by far one of the most
human, even though the 8th Doctor started

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.370
the whole half human thing.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.690
10 was just much more human in his emotinal
states and social habits.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:24.150
He was also one of the more romantically attached
Doctors.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:28.969
He even took the metaphor of being very human
to a literal place when he burned a regeneration

00:07:28.969 --> 00:07:30.909
to create the metacrisis Doctor.

00:07:30.909 --> 00:07:33.900
Who then went off to have his own set of adventures
with Rose.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:40.319
He’s very cheeky but it all seems like an
act to hide this deep sea of anger and regret.

00:07:40.319 --> 00:07:42.159
12 - The Raggedy Man

00:07:42.159 --> 00:07:45.169
The old man in the very young man’s body.

00:07:45.169 --> 00:07:50.430
The 11th Doctor was by far the most anachronstic
in his behavior and costuming.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:56.050
Which might explain why he was so drawn to
helping children.

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.860
He brought back a lot of the eccentric moods
of the sixth doctor but did not include the

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:02.830
more obnoxious egotistical qualities.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:09.909
His most notable catch phrase was of course,
“Bowties are cool”

00:08:09.909 --> 00:08:14.099
and as we learned in Deep Breath, he yearned
for approval.

00:08:14.099 --> 00:08:16.610
As evidenced by his young face.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.080
13 - The Alien

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:23.759
Peter Capaldi’s 12th Doctor is still fresh
out of the gates, so a lot of his finer qualities

00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:25.379
are still percolating.

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:28.939
But he is thus far the most Alien seeming
of all the Doctors.

00:08:28.939 --> 00:08:31.639
Alien in his mannerisms and social habits.

00:08:31.639 --> 00:08:35.769
He still possesses a lot of the pageantry
of the 11th and the seventh doctor with the

00:08:35.769 --> 00:08:38.050
hard edge of the previous doctors.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:42.370
He’s not quite as capricious as Matt Smith’s
Doctor got, but it’s still very early in

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.750
his run.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.250
Give him time.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:52.959
He doesn’t officially have a catch phrase
yet, but thus far “Shut Up” is the leading

00:08:52.959 --> 00:08:54.139
candidate.

00:08:54.139 --> 00:08:58.690
Now big challenge for you guys, describe as
many of the doctor’s as you can just using

00:08:58.690 --> 00:08:59.730
